comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T14:28:44.847Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live open/in-progress lists plus all-status3005-item corpus and request-specific macOS nightly shard search found no exact open shard owner. Full live pm-ul9rye history confirms prior quality/Windows sharding is completed. The existing open broad performance and flake owners remain unclaimed. This leaf owns the newly repeated macOS deadline boundary rather than reopening shipped work. Original jobs118091927156 and118105150893 remain canceled evidence."
  "2026-10-19T14:30:40.637Z","harness:codex","Negative control completed before workflow edits: two focused files report2 failed/52 passed, rejecting the unsharded macOS row and seven-family population. The fix declares macOS24 shards1/2 and2/2 using the already-tested Windows native Vitest shard command, with the same20-minute limit. Reliability tests now cover retired macOS history and new shard alert correlation, preserving original failure denominators. Standard macos-latest runners remain free for this public repository per GitHub's official runner documentation: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-where-workflows-run/choose-the-runner-for-a-job . No larger runner or paid service is introduced."
  "2026-10-19T14:31:27.242Z","harness:codex","Local fixed acceptance passes all54 workflow/reliability tests, four TypeScript projects and focused ESLint. Direct sandboxed Vitest file-only collection proves two shards partition exactly832 project/file identities:416 plus416, zero missing extra or duplicated members. The shared native serial project remains in that population. The first complete unsharded macOS retry passed packed Node/Bun continuation but again reached the20-minute job limit; no second blind rerun was issued. New hosted validation must now prove both declared macOS halves on this change."
  "2026-10-19T14:33:48.454Z","harness:codex","Correction to the preceding population note: Vitest list --filesOnly ignores execution sharding and returned all832 files for each requested half. The aggregation guard rejected that result with832 duplicated identities; it was not a valid partition proof. The54 passing focused tests typecheck and ESLint receipts remain valid. Inspect the installed Vitest execution sequencer and validate its actual split before reporting exact shard membership. The inaccurate earlier statement is retained in history with this explicit correction."
  "2026-10-19T14:34:25.101Z","harness:codex","Correct execution-partition proof now passes: the installed public vitest/node BaseSequencer.shard used by executeTests partitions the complete file-only inventory into416 plus416 project/file identities, with zero missing extra or duplicated members. Source inspection confirms list --filesOnly only enumerates candidates whereas executeTests applies this sequencer before ordering projects. The failed listing-based receipt remains preserved alongside its correction. This proves membership without running or skipping assertions; hosted execution of both macOS halves remains mandatory."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T14:30:43.076Z","harness:codex","A full suite can outgrow a platform job while individual assertions remain valid. Preserve one unchanged retry as evidence, then shard the complete population under the existing deadline and keep retired family history in the recurrence census."
